  message: "STATUS 2026-11-02 (after PR #2004 + PR #2006). KEPT OPEN (todo_hard): the title's condition still holds for the EXACT step, and the acceptance (each member closed on its own repro) is not met.\n\nDONE: phase 1 (measured; numbers above). Phase 2 (#2004): the shared resolvers no longer guess among tied candidates. Phase 3, re-scoped to CALL SHAPE by the phase-1 evidence (locals/params were 2 of 84 wrong edges), first two adopters: Go package-qualified pkg.F() admits no methods (#2004); a Rust method call admits no free function (#2006: on just -241 wrong, +~2,011 correct builder-chain binds, +~136 wrong std binds; aardvark-dns SCIP oracle unchanged).\n\nMEMBER RE-CHECK on dev ae02786fca, each on its OWN filed repro (3 read-only sub-agents, brief + verdicts + fixtures in ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jomik_member_recheck_11022026/; a re-check entry is now on each member): 26 of 27 STILL_REPRODUCE, WI-niriz PARTLY (scala object members now bind; case class / typed-param / nested-type receivers still external). None closed. This is the expected result, not a failure of #2004/#2006: phase 1 predicted it -- the members are per-analyzer scope/typing defects (ocaml local inner fns, python function-local imports and comprehension shadowing, rust/go file- or function-scoped var_types, solidity per-contract scope, starlark load aliases, agda renaming, linker cross-language namesakes, last-write-wins registries), and none of them goes through the tie step #2004 changed.\nFindings beyond their own item, worth acting on: WI-sipoj's two named tests pass only because tmp_path is on tmpfs (ext4 file order gives the wrong binding); WI-dabul (llvm) and WI-povub (js) bind by FILE ORDER (24/24 and 4/8 orderings wrong) -- the same last-write-wins registry, and the next structural target.\n\nNEXT, ranked by measured wrong-edge share (none started):\n1. Call-shape admit adoption, next analyzers: js_ts (member call bound by bare member name: knex path.join -> Builder.join; subject.subscribe), java (suffix ties/exact), then the rest of the method_resolver users.\n2. The last-write-wins registry family (WI-dabul, WI-povub, WI-sipoj, WI-hahud, WI-hubik): a registry keyed by bare name that keeps one entry decides by discovery order -- a core list-valued registry + the #2004 tie rule would turn those into explicit ties.\n3. Per-analyzer lexical scope (INV-hakof, WI-kizih, INV-hovoj, WI-fogoj, WI-nazub, WI-masov): the core position-aware binder (original phase 3) -- unmeasurable on this corpus for ocaml/solidity/agda; measured small for js/python/rust/go."  # bf4f
