  message: "PHASE 3 (call shape), JS/TS ADOPTER SHIPPED: PR #2017 (merged; dev 67318ba81e). Rule: a callee reached through a binding of a module _bare_specifier_is_external positively shows external (Node core, or a registry package the importing package.json declares) is that module's, never an in-repo symbol -- (1) namespace/default/require receiver member (path.join; Case 2 passed the module as a path_hint, but NameResolver applies a hint only AMONG suffix candidates, so a lone in-repo *.join was returned), (2) named or destructured import (const {resolve} = require('node:path')), (3) a method on a receiver whose type is a named import from one (new Subject() from rxjs), unless a catalogued constructor's route applies. Each gets the unresolved edge with the module as hint, so io-boundaries still classifies it. Relative imports, workspace packages and undeclared bare specifiers (tsconfig aliases) resolve as before.\nPRE-REGISTERED A/B (lab ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jomik_jsts_11022026/: PREREGISTER.md, RESULT.md, ab/diff_sites.py, ab/sample_lost.txt), base origin/dev df864cc76a vs the branch, resolved call sites per site with call_lines expanded: express 552 -> 417 (lost 135), knex 11004 -> 8551 (lost 2453), jotai 2073 -> 2066 (lost 7); GAINED 0 in all three; every lost site re-appears as an unresolved edge at the same (src, line) hinted to its external module (2595/2595; hints: chai 2110, path 126, assert 222, sinon 55, lodash 41, ...). Read: seeded sample of 27 lost sites + one example of each of the 32 distinct former targets -- ALL WRONG. Size guess REFUTED (guessed tens): the dominant shape was a destructured require bound to ANOTHER FILE's import binding of the same library (knex expect(...) x2,106 -> test/integration/dialects/oracledb.js:3 `const expect = require('chai').expect`; express path.join x71 -> lib/view.js `var join = path.join`). Some hid I/O: knex child_process.exec(cmd) was bound to a test's `function exec`; fs.stat / fs.existsSync / writeFile to test util fs.js. io-boundaries / verify-claims on knex NOT re-measured.\nRE-VERIFIED on merged dev (cold cache, fixture jomik_jsts_11022026/fx): path.join, rp.delete, path.resolve, destructured resolve, rxjs subscribe -> external module nodes; relative receiver and undeclared '@/builder' alias still bind Builder.join. Production-path tests: packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/tests/test_js_external_receiver_calls.py (5 external shapes, 3 in-tree controls, the INV-fahub deferral behind it); each arm mutation-checked red (via a non-unreachable mutation; an `and False` one trips the mypy gate and leaves a stale log).\nNOT COVERED (open under this item): namespace-constructed receiver (new ext.Cls() then x.m()); test-runner GLOBALS (mocha beforeEach bound to another file's `const beforeEach = sinon.stub()`, phase-1 class D, still reproduces on the fixture); .d.ts declaration targets; dynamically assigned members. NEXT per the ranked list: java call-shape admit; the last-write-wins registry family; per-analyzer lexical scope."  # 0fd2
