  message: "PHASE 3 (call shape), JAVA SHIPPED: PR #2019 (merged; dev 116e1e3039). MEASURED FIRST (lab ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jomik_java_11022026/: PREREGISTER.md, RESULT.md, diff_sites.py, judge_collisions.py, sample.txt). Phase 1's java figure (~38%) was a pooled class rate: its judged java sample is 46 correct / 2 wrong, both suffix ties #2004 already unresolves. Phase 1 never sampled Java's PRIVATE paths (31,609 of jedis's 34,415 edges), so: a seeded sample of 4 per Java evidence path per repo (jedis, commons-compress; 56 edges read): type_inferred, static, direct, inherited, inherited_field all correct; two paths carry the wrong edges, both CORE linkers: inherited_calls Site-2 step 3 (calls -> the receiver's TYPE when the method is nowhere on its in-repo chain; Java only) 3/8 wrong, and method_call_recovery 5/8 wrong, fed by step 3's class edges.\nFIX: step 3 emits `uses` to the type (Java only, _SITE2_TYPE_USE_LANGS), the call stays unresolved. Keeps the controller -> Spring Data repository dependency (e9cf6b75dd, DEEP bakeoff on spring-petclinic) that Java has no other edge for; no longer a class hint for method_call_recovery. A/B dev ba432fd845 vs branch, resolved in-repo call sites: jedis lost 958 (620 calls->type + 338 recovery binds), gained 2; commons-compress lost 184 (182 + 2), gained 0; every lost site re-appears unresolved; 620/182 uses edges appear; no type loses its last incoming edge. Read: lost recovery binds 10/10 wrong on jedis (builder()...build() -> redis.clients.jedis.Builder.build); compress 1 wrong, 1 probably correct; the 2 gained are wrong (another class hint in the same caller -> CommandObjects.build; residual on WI-sudum).\nPRE-REGISTERED AND REFUTED, NOT SHIPPED: Java joining the strict same-name-class guard (variant B: lost 986 / 683, in the predicted range), because prediction 3 failed: of the collision edges it drops, Java's own name rule judges commons-compress 457 correct / 42 wrong. Residual filed: WI-jajaf (java.py stamps an import-resolved receiver_type_id, then Java leaves _LEGACY_SITE2_LANGS). C and D were chosen after B refuted, as the supported subset of B's mechanism.\nProduction-path test test_java_site2_type_use.py (external-base method is a use; the type is no class hint for another call; declared method still resolves; Spring Data dependency kept) + 5 pinned linker/java tests; mutations (edge back to calls; opt-in set emptied) each redden them, the control stays green. Re-verified on merged dev: the fixture's report() has only `uses MyErr`, no MyErr.describe call. Tag kept (quantitative claim). NEXT on the ranked list: the last-write-wins registry family (WI-dabul, WI-povub, WI-sipoj, WI-hahud, WI-hubik); knex io-boundaries re-measure (from the JS PR)."  # 571f
