  message: "KNEX IO-BOUNDARIES RE-MEASURED (the open point of the JS/TS entry, PR #2017). Base dc6725d28e (dev before #2017, worktree with PYTHONPATH pinned) vs dev 116e1e3039 (knex has no Go/Java files, so #2018/#2019 cannot move it); cold caches; hypergumbo io-boundaries --include-tests --json; lab ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jomik_jsts_11022026/iob/. Chains keyed (boundary, io_edge_src, primitive): 1,515 added, 0 removed. subprocess 3 -> 6 (child_process.exec in scripts/build.js exec, and twice in test/jake-util/helpers/migration-test-helper.js -- the exec phase 1 found bound to a test's own `function exec`); fs_read 15 -> 24 (fs.stat, fs.existsSync x7, fs.promises.stat); fs_write 52 -> 53 (fs.promises.writeFile, test/cli/tempfiles.js); external_potential 938 -> 2,440 (chai.expect, lodash, mysql/mysql2.createConnection, stream.on ...). total_io_edges 965 -> 978. So the binds #2017 removed were hiding real crossings, as the phase-1 mechanism said; none was lost."  # 28e0
